    "title": "044: The Decisions Pane: Every Outstanding Decision, One by One, With a Brief, a Recommendation and a Cache"
  },
  "summary": {
    "kind": "quote",
    "span": {
      "end": 2481,
      "end_line": 25,
      "line": 20,
      "start": 1515
    },
    "text": "Decisions reach the operator in several shapes today: an approval card in the inbox, a provisional decision from an optimistic build (`/decisions`), a spec waiting for ratification, a question an agent has left open in a spec, a deadlocked council. The operator wants **one place that lists all of them, one at a time**, each with:\n- a **brief**: two or three sentences saying what it is, and what it adds or changes;\n- a **recommendation** where one can honestly be made (and the plain words \"no recommendation: your call\" where not);\n- a **tick box to accept the default**, for the decisions where a default is safe, so several can be accepted together;\n- a **detail view** with the same brief and recommendation, an accept button, the other choices, and the **normal prompt** so the operator can answer in their own words, with nuance;\n- **no model spend after the first time**: a decision's brief and any conversation about it are produced once and stored (§7)."
  }
}
